course: dictionary
lesson: 11507
title: Ailment: a small illness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An ailment is an illness, usually a minor one. A cold, a cough or a rash are all ailments. When you read an unknown word, look at the words around it, because they often give you clues. «Mum gave Sam a warm drink for his cough, a common ailment.» Sam is poorly, and the cough tells you that an ailment is a kind of illness.
explain: Ailment is a softer, more formal word than illness or disease. You will often meet it in health lessons, in old history books about remedies, and in pharmacies. «The old book listed many ailments and their cures.» Here, ailments means the illnesses people used to have, and cures means what they took to get better.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «She has a rash, a small ailment.» If you swap in illness, the sentence still makes sense, so ailment means illness. Ailment is not a place or a thing you can hold; it is always about health.
fact: An ailment is an illness, usually a minor one.
fact: Common ailments include colds, coughs and rashes.
fact: Ailment is a noun: you can say an ailment or some ailments.
fact: Ailment is softer and more formal than illness or disease.
fact: Ailments are often in health lessons, pharmacies and stories.
exercise: «The nurse gave him a cough sweet for his ailment.» What is an ailment here? | A school trip | A long journey | A type of sweet | *An illness, usually a minor one
exercise: Which of these is an ailment? | A school bag | A new bicycle | A sunny day | *A rash on your arm
exercise: «The old book listed many ailments and their cures.» Find and copy the word that means illnesses. | book | cures | *ailments | listed
test: «Mum gave Sam a warm drink for his cough, a common ailment.» What is a common ailment in this sentence? | A warm drink | A bed | *A cough | A dog
test: Which of these is NOT an ailment? | *A broken window | A cough | A cold | A rash
exam: Which word best means an illness that is usually small? | Garden | *Ailment | Journey | Race
